    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_20051206.0716\n\nWELLINGTON, Dec 7 , 2005\n\nAustralia make 322-5 batting first against New Zealand\n\n\n\n\nAustralia made 322-5 in their 50 overs after Andrew Symonds scored a magnificent 156 against New Zealand in the second match of the Chappell-Hadlee one-day cricket series at Westpac Stadium here Wednesday.\n\nSymonds teamed up with Michael Clarke (82 not out) to put on 220 runs for the fifth wicket.\n\nFor New Zealand, Kyle Mills took 2-60 with all the bowlers suffering from Symonds' onslaught.",
